# High-Fidelity Unified Invoice Printing

## The Issue 📋
The user wants the invoice to look like a "professional bill". Currently, it perfectly replicates the beautiful web UI, but standard business formal invoices lack web-specific traits and instead prioritize stark clarity.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Professionalize [InvoiceTemplate.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/InvoiceTemplate.tsx)
- **Add Title:** Inject a bold `"TAX INVOICE"` header centered at the top to give it formal legitimacy.
- **Sharpen Borders:** Switch the faint `#e2e8f0` (slate-200) borders to a starker `#cbd5e1` (slate-300) or bold `#94a3b8` (slate-400) specifically in print mode to ensure crisp reading on cheap ink printers.
- **Clarify the Footer:** Add explicit T&C or "Goods once sold..." lines if necessary, or just tighten the signature line.
- **Hide Backgrounds:** Remove the `.force-print-bg` from tables so that it is pure white, saving ink and looking much sharper.
